Split into 6 children. Five reuse comparator-accepted declarations with byte-identical frozen types. One is a new leaf under a fresh name: coordinate_minor_continuity = cmcdt_lpi_mwc_coordinate_minor_continuity. This node is at depth 5 with limit 6, so the new child is a leaf. It is provable as one theorem under the frozen imports (Lean evidence below).

Why split. The supplied proof chains six independent analytic obligations, each with a clean reusable interface:
- the Notation and step 1: measurability and uniform bounds of the minors;
- step 2: the L¹ → C_c^∞ reduction;
- steps 3–5: Laplace expansion, Piola identity and integration by parts for smooth maps;
- step 6(i)–(v): mollification with a.e. convergence of derivatives;
- the final paragraph of step 6: formula (3) for Lipschitz maps;
- step 7: the induction P(r).
Five of these already exist as comparator-accepted theorems in the density_one_implies_regular branch, with exactly the statements needed. A node may use only its listed siblings, so reusing them requires listing them as children. Proving everything inline would duplicate about 700 lines of accepted Lean.

