How the children give the selected statement. Only the Notation-level identification of D_t v^i with the derivative of the coordinate function stays in the parent. Fix m, p, r, L, v_j, v₀, a, b and c. Put g^j_s(u) := v_j(u)_{a(s)}, g_s(u) := v₀(u)_{a(s)} and V_t := e_{b(t)} = EuclideanSpace.single (b t) 1.
(1) Each g^j_s and g_s is L-Lipschitz, since |w(x)_i − w(y)_i| ≤ ‖w(x) − w(y)‖ (PiLp.norm_apply_le).
(2) g^j_s → g_s uniformly, because the coordinate map EuclideanSpace.proj (a s) is continuous linear, hence uniformly continuous (UniformContinuous.comp_tendstoUniformly).
(3) Let w be L-Lipschitz (w = v_j or v₀) and let u be a point where w is differentiable; this holds λ-a.e. by Rademacher (LipschitzWith.ae_differentiableAt). There the chain rule for EuclideanSpace.proj (a s) gives fderiv ℝ (x ↦ w(x)_{a(s)}) u V_t = (fderiv ℝ w u e_{b(t)})_{a(s)}. So the integrands c·det of the selected statement and of the child agree a.e., and the integrals agree (integral_congr_ae). They need not agree everywhere: where w is not differentiable, fderiv ℝ w u = 0, but a coordinate may still be differentiable.
(4) coordinate_minor_continuity with k := m, rows g^j and g, directions V and weight φ := c gives ∫ c·det(Dg^j_s V_t) → ∫ c·det(Dg_s V_t). By (3) and Tendsto.congr this is the selected statement.
Inside coordinate_minor_continuity, supplied step 7 runs as written:
- the base case r = 0 is the empty determinant;
- minor_bound and weak_star_l1_upgrade reduce to C_c^∞ weights ψ;
- lipschitz_minor_ibp rewrites both sides;
- T1 → 0 by uniform convergence and the bound B_b;
- T2 converges by the induction hypothesis with the weight ∂_{V_b}ψ·g_0.

